-- #1326 Repro A. `ps.h : Display a => a -> String` and `qs.h : a -> a` are two
-- SIGNATURED, unrelated, same-named bindings. `h` here is unambiguously qs's `a -> a`
-- (`ph` is the alias for ps's); `tag (h NoDisp)` never needs Display. Rejected anyway,
-- at `h`'s own call site, with ps's Display obligation.
--
-- Flattened from the drained must-fail pin's `lib/` layout: this gate's harness copies a
-- case directory's top-level files only (`for f in "$cdir"/*; do cp "$f" "$work/"; done`),
-- so a fixture with a subdirectory silently loses it and BOTH orderings then fail to
-- resolve identically — which this gate would report as "invariant". Measured first-hand
-- while adding this case.
import ps.{h as ph}
import qs.{h}

data NoDisp = NoDisp

tag : NoDisp -> String
tag _ = "ok"

main = println "\{tag (h NoDisp)} / \{ph 5}"
